# Line-ending policy.
#
# Generic type rules come first; the governed-artifact overrides come LAST,
# because in .gitattributes the last matching pattern wins.

*.py                   text eol=lf
*.yaml                 text eol=lf
*.yml                  text eol=lf
*.ts                   text eol=lf
*.md                   text

# Governed byte artifacts must never be line-ending normalized, in either
# direction. Recorded SHA-256 values in sha256_manifest.json and in
# evidence/audit_ec1_2026-08-15/EC1-AUDIT.md are computed over the exact
# provider- or script-produced bytes. With core.autocrlf=true and no attributes,
# Git checked these out CRLF-converted on Windows, so every recorded hash
# mismatched the working tree while matching the index -- breaking the
# verification chain that scripts/merge_coverage_year.py, TA-15, FR-P1-01-4 and
# G-07's matched-artifact evidence all depend on, and making a real tampering
# event indistinguishable from a checkout artifact.
#
# Origin: GOV-2026-08-20-RA-01 finding DATA-01, independently confirmed
# 2026-08-21. Authority: Technical Environment section 13.7 -- exact equality is
# required for hashes, schemas, partition membership, IDs and deterministic CPU
# transformations.

evidence/**            -text
artifacts/**           -text
tests/fixtures/**      -text
